WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:06.319
The final episode of Game of Thrones starts
in the ruins of King’s Landing.

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:10.190
Thousands of people are dead because last
episode, Daenerys burned the city.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:15.090
And now Grey Worm is killing prisoners . He
says that Lannister soldiers are “free men”

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:20.340
who “chose” to fight for Cersei . But
random soldiers don’t really choose – they’re

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.640
forced into war by their lord . Feudalism
is kinda similar to slavery.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.660
But Grey Worm has no sympathy, and kills the
Lannisters.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.710
Tyrion sees the small council room, where
he served in the early seasons.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:39.480
There are so many memories here of Tyrion’s
successes and failures and his family.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.390
Tyrion finds Jaime and Cersei’s bodies under
a surprisingly light dusting of bricks.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.809
Tyrion tried to protect his siblings from
Daenerys , but he supported her war because

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:54.790
he thought she would make the world better
. Now, Daenerys is a tyrant, and Tyrion’s

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.579
family’s dead anyway.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:01.410
So all Tyrion’s work these last seasons
have only brought death to his family and

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.100
to thousands of others.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.079
Daenerys goes full Targaryen.

00:01:06.079 --> 00:01:11.329
She gives a victory speech to her soldiers,
and it looks just like a Nazi rally, with

00:01:11.329 --> 00:01:14.899
Daenerys as Hitler – but with a dragon.

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:19.329
She says she “liberated” the people of
King’s Landing, which is delusional – she

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:22.299
killed those people, after they’d surrendered.

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:27.929
And she says she’ll continue her war, to
‘liberate’ “all the people of the world”

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:32.929
. She mentions Winterfell and Lannisport – threatening
Jon and Tyrion’s family homes.

00:01:32.929 --> 00:01:38.880
She also mentions Qarth – in Season 2, Daenerys
threatened to destroy that city . So Daenerys

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.560
is set to bring death and destruction to the
world.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.020
That flaming spiral in Episode 1 does look
like the Targaryen sigil.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:53.490
Turns out the real threat to the world isn’t
icy white walkers – it’s Targaryen fire.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.919
Tyrion quits as Daenerys’ Hand.

00:01:55.919 --> 00:02:00.590
And his Hand pin looks like Jaime’s hand
– Tyrion refuses to follow the woman who

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.319
killed his family.

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:08.030
Daenerys arrests Tyrion for treason – because
he freed Jaime, and tried to save Cersei .

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:13.360
Arya warns that Daenerys is a threat to Jon,
because Jon is the true heir to the Iron Throne

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.030
. Dany’s also a threat to Sansa, because
Sansa won’t accept her as queen . So Daenerys

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:25.760
is not just a threat to the world, she’s
a threat to Jon, and to Tyrion and their families.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.600
Tyrion tells Jon that Varys was right about
Daenerys – she went bad, and supporting

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.080
her was wrong.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:37.650
So when Tyrion ratted out Varys, he got his
friend killed for nothing . Jon tries to defend

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:42.870
Dany, but Tyrion argues that her massacre
was unjust and unnecessary . Tyrion says that

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:47.450
for the sake of their families and the world
, Jon should kill Daenerys – even though

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:53.950
Jon loves Daenerys . So once again, Jon has
to choose between love and duty . This is

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.310
like when Jon gave up his love Ygritte to
stop the wildlings.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.670
Now, Jon has to kill Dany to save the world.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:06.300
This scene is similar to when Varys convinced
Ned Stark to make a false confession – to

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.500
do something dishonourable to protect his
family.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:14.870
Ned was only convinced when Varys mentioned
Sansa’s safety . And now Jon is only convinced

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:20.801
when Tyrion mentions Sansa’s safety . So
Jon is following Ned Stark’s example, even

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:24.500
though Ned isn’t Jon’s father – Rhaegar
Targaryen is.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:29.190
But as Jon says, people aren’t defined by
their blood – they make their own choices

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:36.200
. And Jon chooses, like Ned, to do the right
thing, even when it costs everything.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.330
Daenerys approaches the Throne.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:43.060
She’s wanted this for eight seasons, and
it’s not quite how she imagined.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.660
She thought the Throne would be bigger, “a
mountain of swords” – and in the books,

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.690
the Throne is much bigger.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:54.210
Daenerys had a vision of the Throne in Season
2, and this scene recreates it.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.630
But this time, Daenerys touches the Throne.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.200
Jon confronts Dany about the killings and
imprisoning Tyrion.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.480
Dany argues that she has to punish Tyrion
for conspiring with her enemies – just like

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:10.480
Jon has killed people who disobeyed him . But
Daenerys has no justification for killing

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.420
the people of King’s Landing.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:17.379
She just says she’ll build a new world , and
that she knows what’s good, and other people

00:04:17.379 --> 00:04:23.110
don’t get to choose . As Tyrion said, Daenerys
has spent years gaining power and killing

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.490
people and being rewarded for it.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:30.560
She’s been surrounded by adoring followers,
people who worship her as messiah.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:36.050
Daenerys once said that what keeps her going
is “faith” in herself . Now her faith

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.680
blinds her to the evil she’s committing.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:44.729
She’s so convinced of her destiny to destroy
tyranny that she’s become a tyrant . Daenerys

00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:50.770
tells Jon to join her, fulfil his destiny,
and rule the galaxy together as nephew and

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:54.039
aunt – and Jon makes his choice.

00:04:54.039 --> 00:04:58.780
They embrace one last time, and Jon stabs
his lover in the heart.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:04.800
It’s like the legend of Azor Ahai, a hero
who sacrificed his lover to save the world.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.979
There are lots of hints in the series that
Jon is this prophesied hero , and it seemed

00:05:08.979 --> 00:05:11.870
as though that meant that he would stop the
white walkers.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:17.259
But in the end, Jon’s destiny is to save
the world from the woman he loves.

00:05:17.259 --> 00:05:22.800
Dany dies in his arms like Ygritte – Jon
chose duty over love.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.389
The dragon Drogon sees Daenerys dead.

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:28.190
She was his mother, she hatched him from his
egg.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:33.719
And a for a moment it looks like he’ll kill
Jon, but instead, Drogon burns the Iron Throne.

00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:37.539
Cause in a way, it was the Throne that killed
Daenerys.

00:05:37.539 --> 00:05:42.219
The Throne represents power, and all the ways
that power corrupts people.

00:05:42.219 --> 00:05:48.599
We saw Cersei and Joffrey and Robert and Stannis
all destroyed by power in different ways.

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:53.650
Wars for the Throne tore Westeros apart, so
the Throne is the real enemy, just as much

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.129
the Night King was.

00:05:55.129 --> 00:06:00.039
By destroying the Throne, Drogon finally ‘breaks
the wheel’ that Daenerys talked about.

00:06:00.039 --> 00:06:05.529
It ends the cycle of conflict in Westeros
– symbolically, at least.

00:06:05.529 --> 00:06:10.830
And the Throne is destroyed in dragonfire,
just like it was originally forged in dragonfire.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:16.569
It’s like the One Ring in Lord of the Rings
– it also symbolises power, and drives people

00:06:16.569 --> 00:06:21.770
mad to possess it, and is destroyed in the
fires that forged it.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.120
Drogon takes Dany’s body and flies east.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.270
Dany thought that Westeros would be her home,
but it never felt like home . The east is

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:35.509
where she found love and success, so that’s
where she returns.

00:06:35.509 --> 00:06:39.720
In her vision in Season 2, Daenerys leaves
the Throne, then goes to be with her dead

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:40.999
lover Drogo.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:45.069
Now, in death, Daenerys returns to her love.

00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:48.199
Weeks later, a meeting is held with the high
lords of Westeros.

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:52.720
There’s Sansa for the north, Edmure for
the riverlands, Robin for the Vale, Gendry

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:58.059
for the Stormlands, Yara for the Iron Islands,
and the new prince of Dorne.

00:06:58.059 --> 00:07:03.419
Grey Worm has Tyrion and Jon prisoner – Tyrion
for his treason , and Jon for killing Daenerys.

00:07:03.419 --> 00:07:08.650
Sansa has brought down an army of northmen
to secure Jon . Davos says the Unsullied should

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:13.050
start their own house in the Reach, which
is a weird suggestion – cause the Unsullied

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:16.529
are eunuchs, so how could they start a noble
family?

00:07:16.529 --> 00:07:21.250
Grey Worm says he just wants justice for the
murder of Daenerys – so you’d think that

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.360
Grey Worm would’ve just executed Jon by
now.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:29.120
Jon murdered Grey Worm’s queen, surely the
punishment is death.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:33.439
Why does he wait around to ask Jon’s family
for their opinion?

00:07:33.439 --> 00:07:39.050
Tyrion says they need to choose a new king
. And Edmure says he’d like to be king . Edmure

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:40.589
is Sansa’s uncle.

00:07:40.589 --> 00:07:45.229
The Red Wedding was his wedding, then he was
imprisoned by the Freys for half the series.

00:07:45.229 --> 00:07:51.309
Edmure’s kind of a doofus, so Sansa makes
him sit . Then Sam suggests democracy.

00:07:51.309 --> 00:07:56.020
He says the King of Westeros should be chosen
by all the people . Some parts of Westeros

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.520
do have elections.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.990
The Night’s Watchmen vote to choose their
leader.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.979
And the ironborn lords elect their king.

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:07.180
But the lords laugh at the idea of giving
peasants a vote – it’s a big step from

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:09.899
feudalism to democracy.

00:08:09.899 --> 00:08:15.690
Tyrion says that stories unite people , and
Bran has a great story . As the magic three-eyed

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:21.439
raven, Bran is the world’s memory, he remembers
the past – so he should lead Westeros in

00:08:21.439 --> 00:08:29.080
the future . And all the lords agree to make
Bran their king . Which is a very weird choice.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:33.810
These lords don’t know Bran, and they don’t
know what a three-eyed raven is – they have

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:37.900
no connection to the magic of the old gods
of the north.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:42.140
Even to his own family, Bran is confusing
and mysterious.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:46.370
To these southern lords, he’s a creepy foreign
cripple.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.880
Bran also has no claim on the Throne.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.230
For the last three hundred years, the Throne
of Westeros passed down a line of succession.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:57.320
That’s why Daenerys had a claim, as the
daughter of the Mad King.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:01.590
Jon Snow has a better claim, as the son of
the Mad King’s firstborn.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:06.420
Jon also has a pretty good story, and he’s
an actual political leader who people know

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.890
and support.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:12.760
Jon’s identity as the true heir to the Throne
was a mystery built up throughout the whole

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:17.250
series , but his claim is not even mentioned
in this scene.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:21.390
Tyrion says they should ignore the line of
succession, cause the sons of kings are often

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.440
terrible like Joffrey.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:28.460
Ending the line of succession is ‘breaking
the wheel’ , it’s stopping a bad system.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.460
But this could also lead to more conflict.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:36.140
Tyrion says that each new king will be chosen
by the lords of Westeros . Which means every

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.720
time a king dies, there’ll be new uncertainty.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:45.440
At least the old system had the stability
of a royal family – now, anyone can be king,

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.930
so it could turn into a free-for-all every
time a king dies.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:53.640
Sansa says that the north will be independent
from this new realm . All the other kingdoms

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:58.380
will be ruled by Bran Stark, but the north
will be ruled by Sansa Stark.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:03.560
This whole meeting is basically a Stark coup
– their family takes over Westeros, and

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:06.520
for some reason, all the other lords agree.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.570
What happened to their ambitions?

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:13.020
In Season 6, Yara made a deal with Daenerys
that the Iron Islands would be independent

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:17.530
. But now she kinda forgets that and agrees
to be ruled by Bran.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:23.180
And Dorne has a long history of proud independence,
and they should be in a strong position now,

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.160
since their armies were untouched in the recent
wars.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:30.190
But this unnamed prince hands his kingdom
to the Starks.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:35.330
This whole story was about ambitious noble
families fighting and scheming for power.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:40.840
But now, in one scene, all the great houses
agree to give up their power to a weird psychic

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:44.180
kid cause ‘he has a good story’.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:48.110
Maybe everyone’s just too tired and confused
to argue right now.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:52.930
But Sansa set a precedent for kingdoms to
secede, so there could be rebellions in the

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.150
future.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:11:00.640
This brave new realm is delicate and uncertain,
but there is hope.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:04.660
King Bran represents a different kind of ruler.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:09.180
Past kings have been bad because they’ve
been proud or cruel or power-hungry.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.330
Bran doesn’t care about power . He has no
pride or cruelty.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:18.150
He barely has a personality – so in theory,
he’ll be fair and unbiased.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:25.490
He’ll be a good ruler because he’s inhuman
– which is a very depressing message.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:30.540
Game of Thrones was always about the struggle
between human good and human evil within each

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:36.190
person . Bran being king suggests that the
solution to human evil isn’t human good,

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:38.420
it’s being not human.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:43.080
And with the failure of Jaime and Daenerys,
this whole season feels deeply cynical about

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.530
the very possibility of human good.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:51.300
Bran makes Tyrion Hand of the King , which
is another strange choice.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:56.330
Tyrion totally failed at being Daenerys’
Hand, and he ended up betraying her.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:02.020
And Tyrion’s widely hated as the Imp – a
kinslayer, kingslayer, and betrayer.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:06.840
It’s hard to believe that any of these lords
even listened to Tyrion at this meeting . But

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:11.740
Bran says that Tyrion will be Hand as punishment
for his crimes – he’ll spend his life

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:16.800
fixing his mistakes .
The Starks want Jon freed, but Grey Worm wants

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.520
justice for Daenerys.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:23.140
So they make a compromise – Jon is sent
to rejoin the Night’s Watch , where he was

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:24.480
in Season 1.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.730
The purpose of the Watch was to defend the
realm from white walkers and wildlings.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:33.080
Now, the walkers are gone, and the wildlings
are friendly, so Tyrion says the Watch will

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:39.530
just be like a penal colony for “bastards
and broken men” . Jon feels guilty and conflicted

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.870
for killing Dany.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:46.130
She was a threat to his family and the world,
but Daenerys trusted and loved Jon.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:52.220
Daenerys was Jon’s queen, and she was his
aunt, which makes Jon a kinslayer – a terrible

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:57.950
crime in Westeros . This makes Jon the last
Targaryen – and as Aemon once said, “A

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:03.410
Targaryen alone in the world is a terrible
thing” . Tyrion says he’ll visit Jon – that

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:07.200
he’ll come and “piss off the edge of the
world” , like when he visited in Season

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.200
1.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.190
We see some Dothraki at the docks.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:15.400
In Episode 3, it seemed like all the Dothraki
died , but apparently many survived to the

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.400
end.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:21.030
These guys were fanatically loyal to Daenerys,
they saw her rise from fire twice – and

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:26.470
they followed her across the world to win
her Westeros – so how’d they react to

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:27.710
Dany’s death?

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:33.250
In Season 6, Dany made all her Dothraki her
blood riders , her sworn protectors.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:38.640
The books say that if a khal is killed, his
blood riders live to avenge him . So surely

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:42.940
when Jon killed Dany, her blood riders would
be honorbound to kill Jon.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.260
But here, the Dothraki just walk past Jon.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.550
They don’t even react to the man who killed
their khaleesi.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:53.490
What are the Dothraki doing now that Dany
is dead?

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:58.170
When Drogo died in Season 1, his khalasar
scattered into warring factions.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:04.270
The Dothraki way of life is to raid and pillage
other people . In Season 1, Daenerys was conflicted,

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:10.180
cause she knew that invading Westeros with
Dothraki would have serious consequences . But

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:15.390
the show never explores how the Dothraki and
Westerosi get along – there’s only one

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:19.310
named Dothraki in Season 8, who only gets
one line.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:25.530
The Dothraki were part of Dany’s story all
series, but in the end they get no closure.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:30.130
Grey Worm and the Unsullied sail to Naath
. Because Naath is Missandei’s home.

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:34.751
They dreamed of returning there together , and
for the Unsullied to protect the Naathi – so

00:14:34.751 --> 00:14:38.610
Grey Worm is honouring his dead girlfriend’s
memory.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:43.940
In the books, Naath has a disease carried
by butterflies that kills foreigners, so hopefully

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.710
that’s not a thing in the show.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:50.030
But now that the Unsullied are gone, who’s
forcing Jon to stay at the Wall?

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:54.520
You’d think most people would be glad that
Jon killed the tyrant who burned King’s

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:55.520
Landing.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:58.180
King Robert pardoned Jaime for killing the
Mad King.

00:14:58.180 --> 00:15:01.960
Why doesn’t King Bran pardon Jon for killing
the Mad Queen?

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:06.630
As the last Targaryen, some people are gonna
wanna make Jon king.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.940
Staying at the Night’s Watch can be a way
of staying out of politics.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:12.870
That’s why Aemon joined the Night’s Watch.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:18.260
Years ago, Aemon was almost made King of Westeros,
but instead, he chose to join the Watch, and

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:23.120
give up his claim, so that his brother could
be king instead . Maybe Jon is staying at

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:27.180
the Watch so his brother Bran can be king.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:30.630
Another sacrifice for the good of the realm.

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:35.240
Jon farewells his family at the docks, like
Frodo in Lord of the Rings.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:40.510
And Sansa apologises for having Jon sent north
. She should probably also apologise for breaking

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:44.340
her oath and revealing Jon’s parentage to
undermine Daenerys.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:49.430
That contributed to the conflict that drove
Dany mad and got Jon exiled – removing Jon

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.670
as King in the North – and making Sansa
queen.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:59.000
Last season, Arya accused Sansa of undermining
Jon so that she can rule the north . And that’s

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.700
kinda what ends up happening.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:06.040
Sansa uses information to create chaos and
climb to power – which is exactly the strategy

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:09.130
used by her mentor Littlefinger.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:14.770
In Season 1, Sansa was a naïve girl who dreamed
of being a queen . But she learned that queens

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:20.320
and princes aren’t as wonderful as she thought
. To survive, Sansa learned politics from

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:25.260
the worst people in Westeros – like Littlefinger
and Cersei and Ramsay , and those people made

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:31.720
Sansa who she is now . So it is a triumphant
moment that someone who was abused for so

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.560
long finally gets power of her own.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.930
And no doubt, Sansa will be a strong ruler
of the north.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:41.640
She won’t make the mistakes that Ned and
Robb and Jon made.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:47.389
But there’s something dark in that Sansa
got here by embracing the lessons of her abusers

00:16:47.389 --> 00:16:52.590
.
Arya says she’s not coming home – she’s

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:58.910
sailing west, to discover new lands , as she
said she would in Season 6 . So Arya is rejecting

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:03.000
a life as a noble lady, and rejecting the
violence of being an assassin.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:08.100
Her story was always intertwined with death
– but now she’s killed the Night King,

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:13.439
she’s defeated death, and she chooses a
life of adventure and freedom instead.

00:17:13.439 --> 00:17:16.319
But she’s also abandoning her family.

00:17:16.319 --> 00:17:21.360
In Season 6, she declared she was Arya Stark,
and her home was Winterfell . But in Season

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:26.220
7, when she tried to reconnect, she ended
up almost murdering her sister.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:30.450
After everything she’s been through, Arya
feels unable to come home.

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:36.760
Like Frodo, she’s damaged, so she’s sails
into the sunset sea – it’s kind of a metaphor

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:37.760
for death.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:41.960
And practically speaking, everyone else who’s
sailed west hasn’t returned.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:48.190
Like this is some Columbus Magellan edge-of-the-world
type shit, and Arya’s not exactly an expert

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.190
sailor.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:52.510
So Arya is letting go of her old lives.

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:56.670
But she keeps Needle – a symbol of her home
and family.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:01.850
Bran makes a weird comment that Jon was exactly
where he was “supposed to be” . At the

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:07.480
council, he hinted that becoming king was
Bran’s destiny all along . Bran has had

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.470
visions of the future before.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:14.080
And it seems like Bran guided recent events
– he gave Arya the dagger than she used

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.500
to kill the Night King.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:20.720
And he told Sam to tell Jon about his parentage
– which divided Jon from Dany, leading to

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:25.830
her death and his exile, clearing the way
for Bran to become king.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:32.010
Like Sansa, Bran spread information that created
conflict that gave Bran power – like Littlefinger

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.010
does.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:37.920
In Season 7, Littlefinger gave Bran Arya’s
dagger, and Bran quoted Littlefinger’s line

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:43.030
that “Chaos is a ladder” . Littlefinger
once said you should see all possibilities

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:48.610
in your mind all the time , which is kinda
what Bran does as the magic three-eyed raven.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:52.160
So did Bran manipulate everything to become
king?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:57.130
It would be pretty evil if Bran knew that
King’s Landing would burn, but he made it

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.130
happen anyway.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:03.790
But that’s exactly the sort of magic Machiavellian
shit that the three-eyed raven does.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:10.270
Like, the previous raven used visions to lure
a crippled boy to a cave full of skulls, and

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:16.580
deleted his personality to make him an avatar
for the magic of the old gods.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:21.440
In the books, the raven is called Bloodraven,
and he has an even longer history of doing

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:26.340
terrible things for the sake of some vague
prophetic greater good.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:29.280
Bran Stark as we knew him is dead.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:33.420
Bran said that he’s not Bran any more , he’s
the three-eyed raven now.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:39.080
So given the raven’s long history of psychic
fuckery, it’s very possible that Bran has

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:46.200
manipulated everyone around him to gain power,
and what we call is Bran is now really a puppet,

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:50.430
a host for the ancient psychic hivemind of
the old gods.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:53.230
What if the raven never gives up power?

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:58.040
The previous raven said he’s been alive
a thousand years , sustained by the weirwood

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.040
roots.

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:03.920
Maybe Bran will become an immortal god-emperor
like in 40K or Dune.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:08.380
Author George Martin’s old sci-fi stories
are full of evil hive minds doing crazy shit

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:09.380
like this.

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:15.070
But the show mostly avoids the high-magic
stuff, so Bran is left ambiguous.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:20.040
What he is and what kind of king he’ll be
is open to speculation.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:24.520
Brienne becomes Commander of the Kingsguard
– the highest and most respected position

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:26.480
for a knight of Westeros.

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:29.240
And there’s a new symbol on the Kingsguard
armour.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:32.070
In Targaryen times, the armour had a Targaryen
dragon.

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:34.070
Under Robert, it was a crown.

00:20:34.070 --> 00:20:37.210
When Tommen joined the sparrows, it was the
Faith’s star.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:40.530
And now it’s a three-eyed raven, to represent
Bran.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:43.700
This highlights again how weird it is to make
Bran king.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:48.670
Cause the raven is a mysterious mystical figure
of the children of the forest and the old

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:53.600
gods, who are only* worshipped in the north
– and the north isn’t even part of Bran’s

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.600
realm.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:21:00.230
This’d be like if the USA used a Canadian
maple leaf to represent their presidency – culturally

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:03.030
and politically it’s just jarring.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:07.660
But as Commander of the Kingsguard, it’s
Brienne’s job to update the White Book,

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:11.070
which records the accomplishments of every
Kingsguard knight.

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:15.920
Jaime’s page had no great achievements , so
he hoped to get some good deeds in there before

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.970
he died . So now, Brienne fills in Jaime’s
page.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:21.330
He took Riverrun peacefully.

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:23.170
He outsmarted Daenerys’ war plans.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.570
And he helped the living save the world from
the dead.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:31.150
Brienne writes that Jaime rode south to save
King’s Landing from destruction, which is

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.740
not really true.

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:35.270
Jaime said he went south to be with Cersei.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.770
He said “She's hateful.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:42.420
And so am I” , and he died saying he and
Cersei are all that matter in the world . Jaime

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:45.440
died hateful, and his redemption failed.

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:50.059
But one of the great lines in the books is
that “Men’s lives have meaning, not their

00:21:50.059 --> 00:21:55.200
deaths” . Jaime’s death was a failure,
but he did great things in his life – and

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:58.010
maybe that’s what matters in the end.

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:02.760
This room is where Jaime gave Brienne the
sword Oathkeeper, and showed her the trust

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:09.050
and respect that she needed – so the legacy
of Jaime’s good deeds lives on even if Jaime

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:11.270
failed in death.

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:16.440
Also apparently Podrick has become a Kingsguard
knight, and it’s great that he’s rewarded,

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:20.830
but Kingsguard knights swear vows of chastity,
they’re not allowed to have sex – which

00:22:20.830 --> 00:22:24.290
seems a terrible waste of Pod the Rod.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:27.870
The small council is the government of this
brave new realm.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:33.050
Tyrion is Hand, Davos Master of Ships, Sam
is Grand Maester, Bronn Master of Coin, and

00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:35.700
Brienne’s there as Commander of the Kingsguard.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:40.309
It’s surprising that Sam is Grand Maester,
cause becoming a maester takes years of study

00:22:40.309 --> 00:22:46.230
– Sam just scrubbed bedpans, stole books
and ran, so is he qualified to represent the

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:47.230
Citadel?

00:22:47.230 --> 00:22:52.580
And maesters take vows of chastity, they’re
not meant to have children and wildling girlfriends.

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:54.390
Maybe the rules have changed.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:58.070
But Bronn as Master of Coin is even more questionable.

00:22:58.070 --> 00:23:00.870
What does he know about responsible fiscal
management?

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:05.740
A few seasons ago, he said himself that he
doesn’t know how loans work . And that’ll

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:10.690
be a problem, cause the Throne owes money
to the Iron Bank – Cersei never paid back

00:23:10.690 --> 00:23:12.710
her Golden Company loan.

00:23:12.710 --> 00:23:17.290
We’ve been warned all series that the Iron
Bank is ruthless – they might start a war

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:22.010
if they don’t get their money . After all
these years of expensive conflict , Westeros

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:27.280
could face financial crisis – and it’s
up to Bronn to prevent this.

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:32.290
Bronn is also Lord of Highgarden, and Lord
of the Reach – Tyrion kept his ridiculous

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:37.190
promise and made Bronn one of the most powerful
lords in Westeros – even though Bronn is

00:23:37.190 --> 00:23:42.460
a disloyal amoral murderer who threatened
to kill Tyrion just two episodes ago.

00:23:42.460 --> 00:23:47.530
There are many powerful houses in the reach
who’ve wanted Highgarden for centuries – they’re

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:51.180
not gonna easily accept Bronn as the overlord.

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:55.820
Tyrion always said that he pays his debts,
and he’s Bronn deserves a reward for eight

00:23:55.820 --> 00:23:57.880
seasons of service to the Lannisters.

00:23:57.880 --> 00:24:02.950
But giving Bronn this much power is not a
recipe for peace.

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:08.020
Sam has a new history book about the recent
wars . It’s called “A Song of Ice and

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:12.179
Fire”, which is the title of the Game of
Thrones book series – it’s how there’s

00:24:12.179 --> 00:24:15.670
a Lord of the Rings book at the end of Lord
of the Rings.

00:24:15.670 --> 00:24:20.400
Thrones author George Martin has said that
that Sam is the character most like him , so

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:24.049
it’s appropriate that Sam presents this
book.

00:24:24.049 --> 00:24:28.000
Tyrion is upset to learn that he’s not mentioned
in the book.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:33.710
Realistically, Tyrion would be mentioned – he
was Hand to a king and queen, he killed Tywin,

00:24:33.710 --> 00:24:35.890
and supposedly killed Joffrey.

00:24:35.890 --> 00:24:40.690
But this is a reference to what Varys said
in Season 2 – that Tyrion will never get

00:24:40.690 --> 00:24:45.360
recognition, and the histories won’t mention
him , because he’s a dwarf and a misfit,

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:47.720
he’ll always be misunderstood and hated.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:53.660
But that only makes Tyrion more heroic for
fighting to make the world better anyway.

00:24:53.660 --> 00:24:58.530
King Bran arrives and says they need a Master
of War , which is ominous.

00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:02.830
The Master of War position was invented by
Cersei . You’d hope that this new regime

00:25:02.830 --> 00:25:07.130
would wanna emphasise peace, not continue
Cersei’s legacy.

00:25:07.130 --> 00:25:12.490
Bran also says they need a Master of Whisperers
, which is a spymaster, like Varys.

00:25:12.490 --> 00:25:16.660
And you’d think Bran could just do that
himself, since he can spy with animals, and

00:25:16.660 --> 00:25:21.910
has visions, and claims to “see everything”
. In the books, the previous three-eyed raven

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:27.120
was once the Master of Whisperers, and used
his magic and spying to basically run the

00:25:27.120 --> 00:25:29.020
realm for decades.

00:25:29.020 --> 00:25:34.060
King Bran really is a continuation of his
legacy.

00:25:34.060 --> 00:25:38.881
Sam says that Drogon is flying towards Volantis
. If he continues that way, he’ll reach

00:25:38.881 --> 00:25:44.910
Valyria – the ruined empire of the dragonlords,
and homeland of the Targaryens.

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:47.190
We saw Drogon in Valyria before.

00:25:47.190 --> 00:25:51.380
So maybe he and Daenerys are going back to
their ancestral home.

00:25:51.380 --> 00:25:55.650
Bran says he might find Drogon with his magic,
but he doesn’t say why.

00:25:55.650 --> 00:25:59.440
Does he wanna make sure that Drogon’s safely
far away?

00:25:59.440 --> 00:26:03.060
Or does the three-eyed raven have some sinister
plan?

00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:08.750
Bran lets the council do the ruling while
he goes and does whatever the three-eyed raven

00:26:08.750 --> 00:26:09.750
does.

00:26:09.750 --> 00:26:14.510
The last line of dialogue in Game of Thrones
is Tyrion telling his joke about the honeycomb

00:26:14.510 --> 00:26:19.000
and the jackass , but once again we don’t
get to hear the punchline.

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:23.799
The scene pans out, and we see the map of
Westeros – it’s cleared of rubble, but

00:26:23.799 --> 00:26:25.540
there’s still a crack in the floor.

00:26:25.540 --> 00:26:28.190
Cause this new realm isn’t perfect.

00:26:28.190 --> 00:26:31.940
There are problems and divisions, and the
king is possibly an evil tree.

00:26:31.940 --> 00:26:37.550
But there are good people in government, and
there’s hope that the wounds will heal.

00:26:37.550 --> 00:26:42.220
The final scene in Game of Thrones has Jon
and the wildlings riding north.

00:26:42.220 --> 00:26:46.881
It seems like Jon is escorting the wildlings,
or maybe he’s abandoning the Night’s Watch

00:26:46.881 --> 00:26:48.480
and joining the wildlings.

00:26:48.480 --> 00:26:53.570
He reunites with Ghost and Tormund – maybe
he’ll spend his life with friends and have

00:26:53.570 --> 00:26:57.190
some fun for once instead of freezing his
ass off on the Wall.

00:26:57.190 --> 00:27:02.620
The scene recreates shots from the first scene
in the series, with rangers riding north.

00:27:02.620 --> 00:27:07.090
These rangers were hunting wildlings, and
got killed by white walkers.

00:27:07.090 --> 00:27:09.280
Winter was rising against them.

00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:14.049
But now, the Watch is friendly with the wildlings,
the walkers are gone, and it seems like winter

00:27:14.049 --> 00:27:15.500
is ending.

00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:20.220
The first line in the Game of Thrones books
is “We should start back” . But as Jon

00:27:20.220 --> 00:27:24.330
and the wildlings ride north, it feels like
they’re moving forwards.

00:27:24.330 --> 00:27:29.660
Things aren’t perfect, but there’s hope
– it’s a dream of spring.

00:27:29.660 --> 00:27:33.940
Author George Martin always said that the
end of Thrones would be bittersweet . And

00:27:33.940 --> 00:27:39.580
it was sweet in the show, to see Brienne knighted,
Sansa crowned, Theon redeemed.

00:27:39.580 --> 00:27:45.940
We got eight seasons of Lannister drama, Daenerys’
conquests, Jon and Arya’s journeys, adapted

00:27:45.940 --> 00:27:49.930
from the books with exceptional production,
acting and music.

00:27:49.930 --> 00:27:54.630
The tv show made some nerdy fantasy books
into the biggest thing in pop culture, with

00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:56.630
a global community of fans.

00:27:56.630 --> 00:27:59.150
[Start showing just S1, fadein other seasons
showing book gap] But it’s bitter that the

00:27:59.150 --> 00:28:01.960
show ended before the book series was finished.

00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:06.180
So for the last few seasons, the showrunners
didn’t have material to adapt.

00:28:06.180 --> 00:28:10.510
They made up their own plots, and tried to
connect them to the book ending that the author

00:28:10.510 --> 00:28:11.680
told them.

00:28:11.680 --> 00:28:15.990
So sometimes there were dumb plotlines like
the wight hunt.

00:28:15.990 --> 00:28:19.890
Sometimes the dialogue was weak cause there
was no book dialogue to use.

00:28:19.890 --> 00:28:24.480
Characters like Daenerys and Jaime had sudden
twists in their stories, which felt rushed

00:28:24.480 --> 00:28:28.150
and undeveloped because they were squeezed
into shortened seasons.

00:28:28.150 --> 00:28:33.720
The politics lost the realism and sense of
consequences that defined the early story.

00:28:33.720 --> 00:28:39.400
And the seasons of built up mystery and magic
kinda went nowhere.

00:28:39.400 --> 00:28:45.500
Complex characters like Varys and Littlefinger
and Cersei became less important, while asshats

00:28:45.500 --> 00:28:51.490
like Euron had huge impacts on the plot without
any character depth to give that impact meaning.

00:28:51.490 --> 00:28:56.770
Stuff happened not as a consequence of character
choices or themes, but simply to surprise

00:28:56.770 --> 00:28:58.290
the audience.

00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:02.930
The main points of the ending on the show
are apparently partly the same as what’s

00:29:02.930 --> 00:29:08.049
planned for the books . But the show’s ending
doesn’t have the same depth and detail that

00:29:08.049 --> 00:29:10.450
gives the books so much meaning.

00:29:10.450 --> 00:29:15.530
So it’s bitter that we didn’t get Daenerys’
conflict with Young Griff from the books.

00:29:15.530 --> 00:29:19.120
We didn’t get the horror of book-Euron and
Victarion.

00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:25.390
We didn’t get the book Dorne plot, with
Arianne and Quentyn, and Alleras in Oldtown.

00:29:25.390 --> 00:29:30.760
Or Sansa with Harry in the Vale, and Barristan
in Meereen, and Marwyn and Moqorro.

00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:36.080
Varys and Illyrio’s Blackfyre conspiracy,
and the northern conspiracy.

00:29:36.080 --> 00:29:39.220
Rickon on Skagos, and Stannis’ Battle of
Ice.

00:29:39.220 --> 00:29:43.559
Lady Stoneheart, Patchface, Strong Belwas,
and Nimble Dick Crabb.

00:29:43.559 --> 00:29:48.530
We didn’t get the full prophecies of Azor
Ahai and the valonqar, the mysteries of the

00:29:48.530 --> 00:29:54.690
white walkers, the Nightfort, Horn of Winter,
ice spiders and a long Long Night, and everything

00:29:54.690 --> 00:29:57.540
else that’ll happen in the next two books.

00:29:57.540 --> 00:30:01.630
Martin recently hinted that the next book
will be out in a year . It’ll be sweet to

00:30:01.630 --> 00:30:02.630
read his ending.

00:30:02.630 --> 00:30:05.350
And it’s sweet that the tv show happened.

00:30:05.350 --> 00:30:10.140
But it’s bitter that the show is not what
it could’ve been.

00:30:10.140 --> 00:30:13.920
Alt Shift X will make more videos on the Game
of Thrones books.

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:16.200
We’ll also make videos on other series.

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:20.540
There are TV shows coming of Watchmen, His
Dark Materials, Lord of the Rings, Wheel of

00:30:20.540 --> 00:30:22.520
Time, and movies of Dune.

00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:26.250
There are also Netflix gems like Dark and
Maniac.

00:30:26.250 --> 00:30:29.620
So these are the kinds of series we’ll make
videos on in future [YouTube cards vote].

00:30:29.620 --> 00:30:32.850
We’ll hold votes and updates on the Alt
Shift X Patreon.

00:30:32.850 --> 00:30:38.070
There’ll also be an Alt Shift Podcast about
short stories – subscribe at the link below.

00:30:38.070 --> 00:30:42.110
There’s also Alt Shift ZZZ for readings
of old books.

00:30:42.110 --> 00:30:49.350
Alt Schwift X is some kind of parody channel(?),
and we don’t endorse it, but it also exists.

00:30:49.350 --> 00:30:53.230
The Game of Thrones fan community has been
coming up with theories and analysis since

00:30:53.230 --> 00:30:58.100
the 90s – places like Westeros.org, and
the subreddit, the Tumblrs, YouTube channels

00:30:58.100 --> 00:30:59.100
and podcasts.

00:30:59.100 --> 00:31:04.580
There are too many to name, but you might
like Glidus for some hard-hitting Australian

00:31:04.580 --> 00:31:07.429
meme-core Season 8 takedowns.

